            ("Independent review, round 3", "The reviewer re-opened ten more company rows and ten more pins (seed 20261024303): 20 of 20 pass. Its wider test of every pin against its own MapPLUTO lot found 18 pins up to 9.7 m outside, pushed past short corner lots by the round-2 26 m rule (860 Broadway's pin sat in front of 862 to 864 Broadway)."),
            ("Own-lot test (review round 3)", f"Every pin is now tested against its own tax-lot polygon (MapPLUTO 26v2, from the planninglabs.carto.com SQL endpoint ZoLa uses, fetched 2026-10-24; cached in _build/out/lots_cache.json). A pin outside moved to its lot's addressed frontage, 3 m inside the lot line: the middle of a corner lot's frontage when it is 35 m or shorter, else the frontage point nearest the old pin (26 m from the cross street on long corner frontages). Whole Foods Union Square's published coordinate sat 17 m outside its lot, so it moved to the nearest point inside. One no-candidate building (33 E 18th St) carries a tax lot on the far side of the street, so its pin stays on the addressed frontage and the bbl is flagged. pin_qa.csv: 419 pins, every one inside its own lot, every testable pin on its block face."),
